data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"Task: implement \\\"greet, tested\\\" in the subject repository.\\n\\nDeliver exactly:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` containing unittest tests that cover:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. asserting `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (e.g. asserting `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Verify locally, in the repo root, that:\\n       python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n   exits with code 0 (all tests pass).\\n\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply with the truth: what you implemented, the exact command you ran to\\n   verify, and its exit code/output. If anything did not work, say so plainly\\n   rather than papering over it.\\n\\nDo not touch any files outside src/greet.py and tests/test_greet.py unless\\nstrictly necessary (e.g. an __init__.py or similar scaffolding required for\\nthe test discovery to work) — if you do, call it out explicitly in your reply.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

